<section class="wrap prose">
  <h2>Why this is harder than it looks</h2>
  <p>Most of us learned the world from Mercator-style maps, which stretch everything near the poles. Greenland looks as big as Africa but is about fourteen times smaller; Alaska looks larger than Mexico but is actually smaller. Areas in this game are total area (land plus inland water) from our atlas dataset. Read the full story in <a href="../guides/map-projections-explained.html">Why every world map is wrong</a>.</p>
</section>
